+## 21. The homepage stopped depending on a third party (Q4, partially)
+
+### F-48 · Three separate Unsplash dependencies before the hero could paint · **P0**
+
+Visible in every `pnpm dev` log across this whole engagement:
+
+```
+GET /api/backgrounds?theme=hero  200 in 8063ms
+GET /api/backgrounds?theme=craft 200 in 8015ms
+```
+
+Not one dependency — three.
+
+**1. `globals.css:978` — a 2400px Unsplash JPEG loaded through CSS `url()`.**
+This was the homepage LCP element and `next/image` could not touch it: no AVIF,
+no responsive `srcset`, no `fetchpriority`, and a DNS lookup plus TLS handshake
+to a third party before the hero could paint.
+
+**2 and 3. `home-client.tsx:449` and `:508` mounted `RotatingBackground` twice**
+— once for the hero, once for the `#services` band. Each fetched
+`/api/backgrounds`, which is where those two multi-second calls came from.
+
+And inside that component:
+
+```js
+useEffect(() => { images.forEach((img) => { const p = new Image(); p.src = img.url; }); }, [images]);
+```
+
+**It preloads every image in the pool** — not the one being displayed, all of
+them, on both instances, on every homepage visit. Then rotates on a 7s/9s timer.
+
+**Replaced with the brand's own surface, drawn in CSS.** `globals.css:419`
+already had `.wood-grain` and `.wood-grain-dark`; the hero now uses the same
+figure tuned for a full-bleed panel, plus a new `.craft-bg` for `#services`.
+Zero bytes, zero requests — the hero paints with the document.
+
+**The two scrim gradients are unchanged.** The comment above them records that
+their stops were measured against the headline position; the layer beneath is
+still a warm dark surface, so they stay valid.
+
+**The dark-theme `filter: brightness(0.72)` was removed from `.hero-bg`** and
+kept on the photographic elements. `.hero-bg` is now built from
+`--surface-deep`, which already flips, so filtering it would darken it twice.
+
+**Q4 is now partially answered, and honestly.** The decision recorded earlier
+was: kill the third-party round trips immediately, and do not fake a photograph.
+That is what this is. When Francisco supplies a real Ecowoods photograph it
+drops in as the last `background-image` layer, or better as a
+`<next/image priority>` behind `.hero-content`, and the scrims keep working
+unchanged. Until then the hero is fast and honest rather than fast and stock.
+
+### The token lint caught this patch while it was being written
+
+The first draft set `background-color: var(--walnut-950)` on `.hero-bg`.
+`scripts/verify-tokens.mjs` — shipped one patch earlier — rejected it and named
+`--surface-deep` as the semantic token for a surface that is dark in both
+themes.
+
+That is the fifth appearance of the primitive violation, and the first one
+caught **before** it reached a commit rather than by a later audit cycle. F-05,
+F-33, F-36 and F-42 each cost a full measurement pass. This one cost ten
+seconds.
+
+### Left in place deliberately
+
+`app/api/backgrounds/route.ts` and `app/components/RotatingBackground.tsx` still
+exist but now have **no callers**. API routes are explicitly out of scope for
+this series, and deleting a component in the same patch that changes the
+homepage's rendering would confuse the blast radius. Both are dead code and
+should be removed in a follow-up that touches nothing else.
